# The formula of success once

The ideal rises are not accidental. It does three things precisely:

** First, the path of the incrementals** was chosen. During the 2019-2023 window period, when the recharge infrastructure was imperfect, the incremental (recharging) perfectly resolved the user’s mileage anxiety. This is the right choice within the time window.

** Second, defines the family SUV class**. "Freaker coloured couch" is more than a tune -- ideal is the first brand to redefine a new energy vehicle from "tech-based super-product" as "home-go-fowl." Accurately locking in 300,000-400,000 family users, a population with a strong purchasing power, a clear demand, a high repurchase rate.

** Third, cost control is extremely significant. In the case of industry losses in general, the ideal is to make a profit by streamlining SKU (early selling only one car) and operating efficiently.

And all three things, all of them, are all of a flying wheel: ** good products ** high-profile <unk> high-volume-out-scale effects <unk> high-morigin resources ** more resources for research and development.

# Why is the ship slowing down?

From 2024, problems were occurring at every link of the flying wheel.

** The incremental process is no longer scarce**. The question world, and the mill, have introduced the incremental mode. In 2025, 7 multinational car companies announced the increase in access. The increase has changed from a unique label to a industry label.

** "Frigerator's Big Sofa" is copied**. Ask the world M7/M9, Snack C16, Ping G9 all started to play home space and smart cabins. Users have a very high value for reproduction.

**800V fast-loading reduces the incremental advantage**. In the second half of 2025, 800V fast-charged and charged with 15 minutes of capacity 300 km. The incremental "refuelling" advantage is significantly reduced.

** Loss of pricing**. Average vehicle prices fell from $330,000** to 2025 **~250,000**, a decrease of **24%** (source: Annual Report). Flagship L9 was listed at a reduced price of 20,000, which was unimaginable three years ago.

** Counterpart view**: There are also arguments that the flying wheels have not broken down — ideal NPS (user recommendation index) remains high at **79.1 **, ranking first in the industry (source: Yearly Motors Journal). Brand mind is still, but only the pain of the product in the product period. The validation window for this argument was in the second half of 2026: if the L series returns and the Maori rate is stable, the wheels are actually only temporarily slowing, not breaking.

